# PROPOSED outcome-to-outcome links for LTU programme TCTEA — a draft for
# teachers to confirm, correct or reject. Not LTU data.
#
# The syllabi state outcomes per course and name prerequisite courses, but not
# which outcome builds on which. The links below were drafted (AI-assisted) from
# the syllabus texts; the reason for each is given in a comment. They are kept
# in their own named graph so they can be reviewed, replaced, or left out of a
# query, and so that every answer that depends on them can be traced to this
# draft. Outcome numbers refer to the generated courses.ttl.
#
# Thread covered: calculus -> linear analysis -> circuits, signals, modelling
# and control -> automatic control -> advanced control / dynamic systems.

@prefix et:      <https://w3id.org/edthread#> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix lo:      <https://w3id.org/edthread/ltu/outcome/> .
@prefix sk:      <https://w3id.org/edthread/skill/> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://w3id.org/edthread/ltu/graph/proposed-threads>
    a prov:Entity ;
    dcterms:title "Proposed outcome links for TCTEA (draft, unreviewed)"@en ;
    dcterms:description "AI-assisted draft derived from LTU course syllabi; to be reviewed by the course teachers."@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://w3id.org/edthread/ltu/graph/courses> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-07T12:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:status "draft" .

# --- Calculus ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Integral calculus (M0066M) builds on differential calculus (M0065M); M0066M
# names M0065M in its entry requirements.
lo:M0066M-4 et:requires lo:M0065M-5 .
# Solving first-order ODEs needs integration.
lo:M0066M-7 et:requires lo:M0066M-4 .

# --- Linear analysis (M0018M, year 2) ----------------------------------------

# Laplace/Fourier transforms are integrals, and complex exponentials appear in them.
lo:M0018M-4 et:requires lo:M0066M-4, lo:M0066M-6 .
lo:M0018M-5 et:requires lo:M0018M-4 .
# Solving ODEs with transforms and the eigenvalue method extends the ODE skills of
# M0066M and uses matrix algebra from M0067M.
lo:M0018M-7 et:requires lo:M0066M-7, lo:M0018M-4, lo:M0067M-3 .
lo:M0018M-3 et:requires lo:M0018M-7 .

# --- Circuit theory (E0003E, year 2) ------------------------------------------
# Entry requirements: "linear algebra, ordinary linear differential equations,
# complex numbers" (naming the retired course M0049M). Mapped to today's courses:
lo:E0003E-1 et:requires lo:M0066M-6, lo:M0066M-7, lo:M0067M-2 .

# --- Signal analysis (S0001E, year 3) -----------------------------------------
# Entry requirements name M0018M Linear analysis; frequency analysis is Fourier analysis.
lo:S0001E-1 et:requires lo:M0018M-4 .
lo:S0001E-2 et:requires lo:M0018M-4, lo:M0018M-5 .

# --- Modelling and control (R0004E, year 3-4) ----------------------------------
# Entry requirements: "Basic knowledge about the Laplace transform, for example as
# acquired in M0018M Linear Analysis" and physics as in F0004T Physics 1.
lo:R0004E-4 et:requires lo:M0018M-4 .
lo:R0004E-3 et:requires lo:M0066M-7 ;
            et:uses lo:F0004T-3 .
lo:R0004E-5 et:requires lo:R0004E-4 .
lo:R0004E-3 et:alignedToSkill sk:mathematical-modelling, sk:simulate-dynamic-systems .
lo:R0004E-5 et:alignedToSkill sk:control-systems-design .

# --- Automatic control (R7003E, year 4) ---------------------------------------
# Entry requirements name R0004E; state-space methods use the matrix exponential
# and systems of ODEs from M0018M.
lo:R7003E-2 et:requires lo:R0004E-4, lo:M0018M-7 .
lo:R7003E-3 et:requires lo:R0004E-5 .
lo:R7003E-3 et:alignedToSkill sk:control-systems-design .

# --- Advanced control design (R7014E, year 4) ---------------------------------
# Entry requirements name R7003E.
lo:R7014E-2 et:requires lo:R7003E-2 .
lo:R7014E-5 et:requires lo:R7003E-3 .
lo:R7014E-8 et:requires lo:R7003E-2 .
lo:R7014E-5 et:alignedToSkill sk:control-systems-design .

# --- Dynamic systems (R7016E, elective) ---------------------------------------
# Entry requirements: mechanics (F0004T), differential equations and the Laplace
# transform (M0018M or a basic control course).
lo:R7016E-1 et:revisits lo:R0004E-3 ;
            et:uses lo:F0004T-3 .
lo:R7016E-3 et:requires lo:M0018M-7 .
lo:R7016E-4 et:requires lo:M0066M-7 .
lo:R7016E-1 et:alignedToSkill sk:mathematical-modelling .
lo:R7016E-4 et:alignedToSkill sk:simulate-dynamic-systems .

# --- Equivalent outcomes between programmes ------------------------------------
# S0004E Signals and systems (TCDAA) and S0001E Signal analysis (TCTEA) state the
# same five learning outcomes, word for word. Proposed as equivalent (closeMatch,
# accepted in place of each other); whether this grants credit is the teachers'
# and the university's decision. Identical wording alone is not enough: the degree
# projects of different specialisations share template outcomes too.
lo:S0004E-1 skos:closeMatch lo:S0001E-2 .   # how an LTI system affects input signals in time and frequency
lo:S0004E-2 skos:closeMatch lo:S0001E-3 .   # implement and simulate LTI systems
lo:S0004E-3 skos:closeMatch lo:S0001E-1 .   # frequency content of a signal
lo:S0004E-4 skos:closeMatch lo:S0001E-4 .   # poles and zeros, in time and frequency
lo:S0004E-5 skos:closeMatch lo:S0001E-5 .   # sampling without loss of information
